hypotheses.statement:
Cup product by $e$ sends $P_kH^m(X)$ into $P_{k+2}H^{m+2}(X)$. For every $i\ge0$ and every $m$, it induces an isomorphism $$\label{norm:relative-hl}
 e^i:\operatorname{Gr}^P_{R-i}H^m(X)
 \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }
 \operatorname{Gr}^P_{R+i}H^{m+2i}(X).$$

Let $H$ be a finite-dimensional vector space over a field of characteristic zero, with finite, exhaustive, separated increasing integer-indexed filtrations $F_\bullet$ and $G_\bullet$. Suppose that $e,f\in\operatorname{End}(H)$ satisfy, for $A_\bullet=F_\bullet$ and $A_\bullet=G_\bullet$, $$e(A_k)\subseteq A_{k+2},\qquad f(A_k)\subseteq A_{k-2}.$$ Assume that the induced raiser on each associated graded is Lefschetz with the same center $r$, and that $$\label{alg:double-commutator}
 [[f,e],e]=-2e,
 \qquad [u,v]=uv-vu.$$ Then $F_k=G_k$ for every integer $k$. If $H$ has a further grading respected by both filtrations, and $e,f$ have degrees $2,-2$ for that grading, the equality holds degree by degree.

The morphism $Y^{\mathrm B}\to V$ is smooth of relative dimension $2R+2b$. There is a correspondence $$X^{\mathrm B}\xleftarrow{\ \pi\ }Z^{\mathrm B}
 \xrightarrow{\ \iota\ }Y^{\mathrm B}_q,$$ where $Z^{\mathrm B}$ imposes $\nu=\zeta I$ and $\pi$ is the full flag bundle. The map $\iota$ is a regular embedding of codimension $b$ with normal bundle $T_\pi^*$. The cohomological operators $$\mathsf A=\pi_*\iota^*,\qquad
 \mathsf B=\iota_*\pi^*$$ have degrees $-2b$ and $2b$, respectively, and satisfy $$\label{betti:split}
 \mathsf A\mathsf B=(-1)^b n!\,\mathrm{id}.$$ Here and below a covariant star denotes the Gysin map.

Assume the Hodge–Tate hypothesis of Proposition <a href="#diag:variation" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="diag:variation">10</a>. The combined monodromy action on all $\operatorname{Gr}^W_aH^j(\mathscr H_t,\mathbb Q)$ has finite image. For any loop with cohomology monodromy $T$, there is an integer $M>0$ such that $T^M$ is unipotent and $$\label{diag:log}
  N=\frac{1}{M}\log(T^M)
  \quad\text{satisfies}\quad N(W_a)\subset W_{a-2}.$$ The logarithm is a finite polynomial. On the total cohomology ring, $N$ is a derivation of cohomological degree zero.

For the translation $T:Y_{0,v}\to Y_{0,v}$ associated with $\ell=(1,-1,0,\ldots,0)$ and every integer $k\ge0$, $$\label{calc:translation-polynomial}
 T^{k*}e_{\mathcal Y}=e_{\mathcal Y}+ky+k^2t_C.$$ Consequently the logarithm from Section <a href="#sec:translation" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="sec:translation">6</a> satisfies $$\label{calc:logarithm}
 N(e_{\mathcal Y})=y$$ on $H^*(\mathcal Y,\mathbb Q)$ and, by restriction, on every fiber.

Let $\pi:\operatorname{Fl}(V)\to B$ be the full-flag bundle of a rank-$n$ complex vector bundle, and let $w_1,\ldots,w_n$ be its formal Chern roots. For [(calc:permutation)](#calc:permutation) a polynomial $F$ in the first Chern classes of the ordered flag lines, $$\pi_*\bigl(F(Q_\bullet)c_b(T_\pi)\bigr)
   =\sum_{\sigma\in\mathfrak S_n}
      F(w_{\sigma(1)},\ldots,w_{\sigma(n)}).$$ If $\sum_i\ell_i=0$, then $$\label{calc:permutation}
 \sum_{\sigma\in\mathfrak S_n}
       \left(\sum_i\ell_iw_{\sigma(i)}\right)^2
 =n(n-2)!\|\ell\|^2
    \left(\sum_iw_i^2-\frac{(\sum_iw_i)^2}{n}\right).$$ Both identities, when their expressions are invariant under common translation of the roots, hold for the associated flag bundle of a principal $\mathrm{PGL}_n$-bundle with rational coefficients.

Let $\delta=\deg(x:S\to C)$. The operator $f'$ of <a href="#trans:fprime" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="trans:fprime">[trans:fprime]</a> satisfies $$\label{calc:scalar}
 [[f',e],e]=8(-1)^b n(n-2)!\delta\,e.$$ Consequently $$\label{calc:f}
 f=\frac{(-1)^{b+1}}{4n(n-2)!\delta}\,f'$$ has cohomological degree $-2$, lowers perversity by two and Betti weights by four, and satisfies $[[f,e],e]=-2e$.

